 Photo_Chat_Design_2] Dristin Watson (you) · 10:30 AM: Great 🔥 That’s a nice design idea. 😍👏 Milie Nose · 8:20 PM: Awesome 🔥\",\"text\":\"Killan James · 10:12 AM: Hi, are you still a web designer? / Would love to see some designs 😁\\n— Today, March 24 —\\nClaudia Maudi · 10:30 AM: Hey, happy to hear from you. Yes, I will be back in a couple of days. / Here are some designs I took earlier today. [Photo_Chat_Design_1, Photo_Chat_Design_2]\\nDristin Watson (you) · 10:30 AM: Great 🔥 That’s a nice design idea. 😍👏\\nMilie Nose · 8:20 PM: Awesome 🔥\"},{\"id\":\"7:88\",\"name\":\"Attachments (06)\",\"text\":\"Attachments (06)\"},{\"id\":\"7:89\",\"name\":\"Very important file.figma · Some file.scratch · List of something.xd · Very important file.svg — each 7.5 MB · 3.22.22, 11:15 AM\",\"text\":\"Very important file.figma · Some file.scratch · List of something.xd · Very important file.svg — each 7.5 MB · 3.22.22, 11:15 AM\"},{\"id\":\"7:91\",\"name\":\"What is fixed · what is yours\",\"text\":\"What is fixed · what is yours\"},{\"id\":\"7:94\",\"name\":\"Fixed (given)\",\"text\":\"Fixed (given)\"},{\"id\":\"7:95\",\"name\":\"• Frame list and exact names • Must-include content per frame (what, not how) • Navigation structure and links • All data and copy • Brand color #5051F9 and DM Sans • Media: logo, avatars, photos, icons • Default Button, default Text Field\",\"text\":\"• Frame list and exact names\\n• Must-include content per frame (what, not how)\\n• Navigation structure and links\\n• All data and copy\\n• Brand color #5051F9 and DM Sans\\n• Media: logo, avatars, photos, icons\\n• Default Button, default Text Field\"},{\"id\":\"7:97\",\"name\":\"Yours (designer decides)\",\"text\":\"Yours (designer decides)\"},{\"id\":\"7:98\",\"name\":\"• Layout, grid, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen • All other colors: neutrals, text, surfaces, chart and bar colors, tag colors, status / progress colors, online status, error / disabled • Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation • All states: current nav item, current period tab, current settings tab, current conversation, unread, typing, hover, focused field • Sidebar, top bar, stat cards, charts, task rows, schedule card, message rows, gantt rows and bars, kanban columns and cards, chat bubbles, folders, file table, storage panel, profile header, tabs, form, contact panel • How avatars, covers and photos are cropped\",\"text\":\"• Layout, grid, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen\\n• All other colors: neutrals, text, surfaces, chart and bar colors, tag colors, status / progress colors, online status, error / disabled\\n• Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation\\n• All states: current nav item, current period tab, current settings tab, current conversation, unread, typing, hover, focused field\\n• Sidebar, top bar, stat cards, charts, task rows, schedule card, message rows, gantt rows and bars, kanban columns and cards, chat bubbles, folders, file table, storage panel, profile header, tabs, form, contact panel\\n• How avatars, covers and photos are cropped\"},{\"id\":\"7:100\",\"name\":\"How it is evaluated\",\"text\":\"How it is evaluated\"},{\"id\":\"7:101\",\"name\":\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\",\"text\":\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\"},{\"id\":\"7:102\",\"name\":\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data & copy accuracy 3. Flow & prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality & consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (current nav, tabs, conversation, unread / typing)\",\"text\":\"1. Checklist coverage per frame\\n2. Data & copy accuracy\\n3. Flow & prototype completeness\\n4. Information hierarchy\\n5. Visual quality & consistency of your own system\\n6. Component reuse\\n7. State design (current nav, tabs, conversation, unread / typing)\"},{\"id\":\"7:103\",\"name\":\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 6 named frames, your components and the prototype.\",\"text\":\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 6 named frames, your components and the prototype.\"}]"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06fbff5f-a7f3-4edc-8cf6-ab7b50201e39","uuid":"62ccc0d5-23c5-4d31-9d33-7ddf98417484","timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:14:16.963Z","tool_use_result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[{\"id\":\"7:4\",\"name\":\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\",\"text\":\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\"},{\"id\":\"7:5\",\"name\":\"OCTOM — team task management web app\",\"text\":\"OCTOM — team task management web app\"},{\"id\":\"7:6\",\"name\":\"Design a team task-management web app: see today’s overview, plan the project timeline, move tasks on a board, manage files, edit your profile and chat with the team. Desktop web app, 1440 × 1024, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\",\"text\":\"Design a team task-management web app: see today’s overview, plan the project timeline, move tasks on a board, manage files, edit your profile and chat with the team. Desktop web app, 1440 × 1024, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\"},{\"id\":\"7:8\",\"name\":\"How to work\",\"text\":\"How to work\"},{\"id\":\"7:9\",\"name\":\"1. Build exactly the 6 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The brand color and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and a default Text Field. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the logo, the avatars, the photos and the icons from 04 · Media. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\",\"text\":\"1. Build exactly the 6 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links.\\n2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions.\\n3. The brand color and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently.\\n4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button and a default Text Field. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\\n5. Use the logo, the avatars, the photos and the icons from 04 · Media.\\n6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\"},{\"id\":\"7:11\",\"name\":\"Frames · goals · must include · links\",\"text\":\"Frames · goals · must include · links\"},{\"id\":\"7:12\",\"name\":\"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\",\"text\":\"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\"},{\"id\":\"7:15\",\"name\":\"01_Dashboard\",\"text\":\"01_Dashboard\"},{\"id\":\"7:16\",\"name\":\"Goal: See today’s workload, schedule and messages at a glance.\",\"text\":\"Goal: See today’s workload, schedule and messages at a glance.\"},{\"id\":\"7:17\",\"name\":\"MUST INCLUDE\",\"text\":\"MUST INCLUDE\"},{\"id\":\"7:18\",\"name\":\"• Messages: “Messages” · 4 conversations, each with avatar, name and last message (see DATA) • New Task: “New Task” · more (Icon_More) · “Task Title” · field “Create new” · emoji row 🎉 😍 😁 🔥 😘 😉 😎 👩 🙄 · “Add Collaborators” · chips Angela · Chris (each with an avatar) · add (Icon_Plus) · send (Icon_Send) • Sidebar: Logo_Octom · “OCTOM.” · icon navigation Dashboard (Icon_Nav_Dashboard) · Timeline (Icon_Nav_Timeline) · Task (Icon_Nav_Task) · Settings (Icon_Nav_Settings) · Messages (Icon_Nav_Messages) · Files (Icon_Nav_Files) · current: Dashboard • Stats: Task Completed 08 · New Task 10 · Project Done 10, each with icon, trend line and change “10+ more / 10+ more / 08+ more from last week” • Task Done: “Task Done” · Daily · Weekly · Monthly · current: Monthly · line chart with two series, y axis 0 – 400, months May – Apr (values illustrative) • Tasks: “Task” · 2 task rows, each with play (Icon_Play), “Start from” and time (Icon_Clock), title, link (Icon_Link), comments (Icon_Comment), progress and “Reminder” (Icon_Bell) (see DATA) • Today’s Schedule: “Today’s Schedule” · “30 minute call with Client” · “+ Invite” · “Project Discovery Call” · 3 participant avatars + initials “R” · timer 28:35 · call (Icon_Phone) • Top bar: search field “Search anything...” (Icon_Search) · notifications (Icon_Bell) with count 2 · Avatar_Current_User · account menu (Icon_Chevron_Down)\",\"text\":\"• Messages: “Messages” · 4 conversations, each with avatar, name and last message (see DATA)\\n• New Task: “New Task” · more (Icon_More) · “Task Title” · field “Create new” · emoji row 🎉 😍 😁 🔥 😘 😉 😎 👩 🙄 · “Add Collaborators” · chips Angela · Chris (each with an avatar) · add (Icon_Plus) · send (Icon_Send)\\n• Sidebar: Logo_Octom · “OCTOM.” · icon navigation Dashboard (Icon_Nav_Dashboard) · Timeline (Icon_Nav_Timeline) · Task (Icon_Nav_Task) · Settings (Icon_Nav_Settings) · Me